 ## Subtopics
 
 ### Entropy Prior
-Uses the negative entropy of the opacity distribution. Tends to lose thin materials (e.g., flow tails) more than the Beta prior [S1]. [Link](entropy-prior.md)
+Applies a negative entropy regularization to the opacity distribution. Tends to lose thin materials (e.g., flow tails) more than the Beta prior [S1]. Choose when maximum entropy reduction is acceptable and computational simplicity is prioritized. [Link](entropy-prior.md)
 
 ### Dream Field Prior
-Applies a prior on mean transmittance. Changes are less clear compared to Beta and Entropy priors [S1]. [Link](dream-field-prior.md)
+Applies a prior on mean transmittance rather than final opacity. Changes to the rendered output are less clear compared to Beta and Entropy priors [S1]. Choose when transmittance-based regularization better matches the scene's physical properties. [Link](dream-field-prior.md)
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(P)$, where $P$ is the number of pixels, as it requires a single pass over the rendered opacity image.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(P)$ to store the intermediate log terms, or $O(1)$ if computed incrementally.
